why I used logging:
1. structured tracking
2. I use it for debugging especially when I am making production grade projects
3. I use it for Error Diagnosis
4. Logging helps with audit and monitoring

why I imported list, dict and optional

1. Defines the exact structure for st.session_state.messages, a list of dictionaries containing string keys (role, content) and string values.

2. Explicitly shows that a function returns a str on success or None on failure/error.

3. Enables automatic type checking (MyPy/Pylance) and provides accurate IDE autocompletion.

4. Makes function inputs and return types clear instantly without needing extra comments.


I also managed to use side bars and dividers via stream lit documentations https://docs.streamlit.io/.

I am using Gemmma Model dubbed Saimon in this project. 